When I use ddply on a data frame with approximately 25k rows, it keeps using memory until it gets to 80% of available memory and then it seems like my Linux system throttles CPU usage to less than 2%.  I'm trying to prepare a data frame for casting from long to wide per this instruction <http://stackoverflow.com/a/12831856/3810211>.

The data frame:

> > head(yat3)
>   sch_no grade subject mean
> 1   6730     3    Math   NA
> 2   6730     3 Reading   NA
> 3   6730     4    Math   NA
> 4   6730     4 Reading   NA
> 5   6730     4 Writing   NA
> 6   6730     5    Math   NA

> > nrow(yat3)
> [1] 25592

The command:

> tmp <- ddply(yat3, .(sch_no, grade), transform, newid = paste(sch_no, grade))

If I issue the following command it finishes promptly:

> yat3$newid <- paste(yat3$sch_no, yat3$grade)

Am I doing something wrong?   Or is this a bug?

Thanks!

